<h2 class="h2">Arrivals at FLL</h2>
<div class="rule"></div>
<p>Your chauffeur tracks the flight and adjusts to early or delayed arrivals, then meets you curbside or at a pre-arranged meet-and-greet point inside the terminal — confirmed at booking, by your specific terminal (FLL runs Terminals 1 through 4, each with its own curb). A reasonable buffer for customs delays is factored into the pickup plan — ask us to confirm current wait-time terms when you book.</p>
<h2 class="h2" style="margin-top:40px">To Aventura, Sunny Isles, Las Olas &amp; South Florida</h2>
<div class="rule"></div>
<p>FLL to the Aventura/Sunny Isles corridor typically runs 25-35 minutes outside peak hours — this is close to our home base, so timing and routing are well established, not a guess based on a map app. FLL to Las Olas and downtown Fort Lauderdale is closer still, typically 10-15 minutes.</p>
</div>
<div class="prose reveal">
<h2 class="h2">Fixed quote, confirmed first</h2>
<div class="rule"></div>
<p>Every FLL transfer is quoted at a fixed price before the trip, tolls and standard wait time included. No surge pricing, no reassigned driver mid-trip.</p>
<h2 class="h2" style="margin-top:40px">Cruise connections</h2>
<div class="rule"></div>
<p>Continuing on a cruise from Fort Lauderdale? FLL sits minutes from Port Everglades, and we handle cruise-sized luggage as a matter of course. Flying in the day before your sailing rather than same-day removes the single biggest source of missed-boarding risk — worth considering for any cruise with a fixed departure time. We also cover <a href="airport-transfers.html" style="color:#B8912E;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:500">MIA and DJT transfers →</a>, plus PortMiami cruise pickups.</p>
<p style="margin-top:16px">Rideshare or a pre-booked chauffeur at FLL? See our <a href="blog-private-chauffeur-vs-rideshare.html" style="color:#B8912E;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:500">Uber vs. private car service comparison →</a></p>
<p style="margin-top:16px">Staying in Fort Lauderdale, not just passing through? See <a href="fort-lauderdale.html" style="color:#B8912E;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:500">Fort Lauderdale coverage →</a></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
