<details><summary>Where at FLL do you meet arriving passengers?<span class="pm">+</span></summary><div class="ans">Curbside at arrivals by default, or a meet-and-greet point past baggage claim if you'd rather not manage bags to the curb alone — confirmed with you when you book.</div></details>
<details><summary>How does Onyx handle a delayed or early FLL landing?<span class="pm">+</span></summary><div class="ans">Your chauffeur tracks the flight in real time and adjusts the pickup window automatically, at no change to the fixed quote you were given at booking.</div></details>
<details><summary>Do you cover Port Everglades cruise transfers from FLL?<span class="pm">+</span></summary><div class="ans">Yes. FLL-to-Port Everglades is a short, well-established run for us given how close the airport sits to the port, timed against your ship's boarding window.</div></details>
<details><summary>Is FLL usually faster than MIA for South Florida arrivals?<span class="pm">+</span></summary><div class="ans">For the Aventura/Sunny Isles corridor, yes in most cases — FLL tends to run 25–35 minutes versus MIA's 25–40, and FLL generally sees less airport-access congestion. Fort Lauderdale and Boca Raton destinations naturally favor FLL further still.</div></details>
<details><summary>Can I book a standing weekly or seasonal FLL pickup?<span class="pm">+</span></summary><div class="ans">Yes. Recurring FLL pickups for seasonal residents or frequent business travelers are arranged the same way as a one-off transfer, with the same chauffeur held for the standing schedule where possible.</div></details>
</div>
